<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Calgacus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Calgacus was a Caledonian leader who, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>, led the peoples of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> against the Roman governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gnaeus-julius-agricola">Agricola</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mons-graupius">Battle of Mons Graupius</a> in 83 or 84 CE. Tacitus gives him a famous speech against Roman imperialism, ending 'they make a desert and call it peace'. He is the first person in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> known by name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/calgacus.jpg" alt="Calgacus" width="320" height="328" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Not given in text, but viewable on the sketch · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calgacus.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
